    "Documentation (U1) is authored in the project's existing Asciidoctor format and integrated into the reference guide so it is rendered alongside the rest of the Spring Cloud Data Flow documentation.",
    "Maintain Java 17+ baseline and avoid introducing dependencies that are not already used by the project."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The developer is a single experienced engineer familiar with Spring Framework, Spring Cloud Stream, and Spring Cloud Data Flow internals.",
    "The Lattice, YARN, and CC SPI modules already have a baseline of existing tests; the work is incremental coverage rather than building the test suites from scratch.",
    "Test infrastructure (embedded servers, Docker images for YARN/Lattice/CC, or stubs) is already partially available in the repository and can be reused.",
    "The container shutdown bug (U7) is reproducible in the development environment using the provided stream definition.",
    "A CI pipeline is available and configurable to run the new integration tests; pipeline file edits are within scope.",
    "No new third-party libraries need to be introduced; everything required can be expressed with the existing dependency set.",
    "User stories U2, U3, U4, U6 cover the same SPI module's unit and integration test work as U5 and are estimated at similar effort unless the SPI's complexity differs materially.",
    "The multiple binder connection factory feature (U8) is implemented as a configurable enhancement with default behavior unchanged, so existing single-binder deployments continue to work without modification.",
    "All estimates are net productive engineering hours (coding, designing, debugging, reviewing, and validating) and exclude calendar waiting time, meetings beyond a normal review cadence, and unrelated overhead."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Project familiarization and environment setup",
      "activity_description": "Read and understand the relevant modules (Lattice, YARN, CC SPI implementations, Spring Cloud Stream binder factory, Admin UI shutdown flow, BOM template code) and prepare the local build/test environment including CI configuration access.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Document BOM template usage (U1)",
      "activity_description": "Author reference documentation for BOM templates, including how to declare and use them to include external libraries dynamically. Add worked examples, place content in the existing Asciidoctor reference guide, and verify the generated docs build cleanly.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Enhance Lattice SPI unit test coverage (U5)",
      "activity_description": "Add new JUnit/Mockito-based unit tests targeting previously untested Lattice SPI classes and branches to raise coverage and provide immediate CI feedback on regressions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Enhance Lattice SPI integration test coverage (U2)",
      "activity_description": "Add Spring-based integration tests that exercise Lattice SPI end-to-end against an embedded/Lattice test runtime so the CI pipeline can continuously evaluate functionality.",
      "most_likely_effort": 18
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Enhance YARN SPI unit test coverage (U6)",
      "activity_description": "Add new JUnit/Mockito-based unit tests for YARN SPI classes and branches, focusing on application submission, resource allocation, and lifecycle logic.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Enhance YARN SPI integration test coverage (U4)",
      "activity_description": "Add integration tests that drive YARN SPI through a real (or testcontainer-based) YARN runtime, including deploy/undeploy paths so CI can continuously evaluate functionality.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Enhance CC SPI integration test coverage (U3)",
      "activity_description": "Add integration tests that exercise the Cloud Foundry SPI, including deployment and undeploy flows, configured to run in the CI pipeline for continuous evaluation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 18
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Fix container shutdown bug from Admin UI (U7)",
      "activity_description": "Reproduce the issue with the supplied JDBC source → HDFS sink stream, diagnose why the container cannot be shut down from the Admin UI, implement a targeted fix, and add a regression test that prevents the issue from recurring.",
      "most_likely_effort": 14
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "Implement multiple binder connection factory support (U8)",
      "activity_description": "Design and implement the ability to configure and use more than one binder connection factory in Spring Cloud Stream so producers and consumers can mix and match binders per channel. Includes API/configuration changes, binder factory refactoring, default-fallback behavior, unit and integration tests, and reference documentation updates.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Code review, final integration, and CI verification",
      "activity_description": "Submit pull requests, address review comments, ensure all new and existing tests pass locally, verify the CI pipeline runs the new integration tests successfully, and perform a final end-to-end smoke test of the increment.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 154
  }
}
